35:T1083,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What are the best free SEO tools?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The best free SEO tools cover the four jobs that move rankings: keyword research, on-page SEO, technical SEO and backlinks. This toolbox has all four in one place: a keyword research tool with real search volume and difficulty, title tag and alt text generators, a Google crawler simulator, robots.txt and sitemap checkers, a Google rank checker and a backlink checker. Pair them with Google Search Console for your own site's data."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are these SEO tools really free?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Every tool is free with no signup, no credit card and no email gate. Tools that use paid data, like keyword research, the backlink checker and the rank checker, have a fair hourly limit per visitor so they stay free for everyone."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I do SEO for free?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. You can research keywords, write better titles and meta tags, fix crawl issues and check your rankings and backlinks without paying for software. Free SEO tools plus Google Search Console cover most of what a small site needs. What SEO really costs is time: writing helpful content and earning links."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I do SEO on my own?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Start with keyword research to pick topics people search for, write one page per topic, give each page a clear title tag and meta description, make sure Google can crawl it, and earn a few links from relevant sites. The free tools here walk you through each step, and the SEO checklist puts them in order."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I check the SEO of my website?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Run your key pages through the website metadata checker for titles, descriptions and social tags, the Google crawler 